--- a/docs/reference.md
+++ b/docs/reference.md
@@ -87,7 +87,7 @@ term that follows it, so `W/m^2/K` is watts per square metre per kelvin.
 |---|---|---|
 | `json.fields` | `input, value, unit, text` | keys of the object |
 | `json.value` | `number` | the converted value, rounded as in `text` |
-| `json.unit` | `symbol` | the target unit's symbol |
+| `json.unit` | `{symbol, name}` | an object with the target unit's symbol and its singular name, as in `{"symbol": "km", "name": "kilometre"}` |
 
